[0.556,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;231mwhen an issue gets the \u001b[38;5;153magent\u001b[38;5;231m label: it reads the issue, makes the fix on a new branch,\u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mand opens a pull request with it for us to review. The API key is in the repository \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231msecret \u001b[38;5;153mANTHROPIC_API_KEY\u001b[38;5;231m.\u001b[39m                                                               \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246mThought for \u001b[1m3m 10s\u001b[22m, searched for \u001b[1m4\u001b[22m patterns, read \u001b[1m8\u001b[22m files, listed \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m directories, ran \u001b[1m19\u001b[22m \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bshell commands \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[39m Now I have what I need. Let me write the workflow. The key constraint from \u001b[38;5;153mLOOPS.md\u001b[39m/the\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  guard is that the job reading the issue must be read-only with no token, so the push/PR\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  happens in a second job; and egress is blocked, so the change crosses between them as a\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  job output rather than an artifact (artifact upload would require wildcard blob hosts\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  the guard forbids).\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;114m●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mWrite\u001b[22m(.github/workflows/agent-fix.yml)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  ⎿  \u001b[39mWrote\u001b[12G\u001b[1m165\u001b[16G\u001b[22mlines\u001b[22Gto\u001b[25G\u001b[1m.github/workflows/agent-fix.yml\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m  1 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;242m# Drafts a fix when an issue is labeled `agent`, then opens a draft pull r\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;242mequest for review.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m  2 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;242m#\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m  3 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;242m# The job that reads the issue runs Claude Code. It holds no GitHub token \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;242mthat can write, the issue text reaches it\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m  4 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;242m# only as a file (through `env:`, never through `${{ }}` in a command or p\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;242mrompt), and its egress is filtered. The\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m  5 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;242m# change crosses to a second job as a compressed, base64-encoded job outpu\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;242mt, and only that second job has the token\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m  6 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;242m# that pushes the branch and opens the pull request.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m… +159 lines \u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H\u001b[H\r\u001b[27B\u001b[38;5;174m✽\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
